# NOTE: this file previously held two different .gitignore versions
# concatenated together, with contradictory rules. The old top half ignored
# `triage_model/`, `*.pkl` and `embedding_*.csv` - which are exactly the
# artifacts this repo SHIPS. The effect was that anyone who retrained saw a
# clean `git status` and their updated model was silently never committed,
# while the bottom half's own comment said those CSVs "ARE tracked".
# Deduplicated, and the rules that shadowed tracked deliverables removed.

# Python virtual env
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints

# Hugging Face / sentence-transformers model cache (if downloaded into the project)
.cache/
hf_cache/
huggingface/
models--*/

# Generated prediction outputs (recreated by predict_batch.py)
*_predictions.csv
*_predictions.xlsx

# Captured console logs from local runs. The model artifacts in
# triage_model/ and the *_results.csv tables ARE tracked deliverables and
# must stay visible to git.
eval_out.txt
eval_raw.txt

# Editor temp
*.swp
*.swo

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local version snapshots of the model bundle, kept for rollback while
# iterating. The LIVE bundle in triage_model_embedding/ is the tracked
# deliverable; these dated copies are local-only and would bloat the repo.
triage_model_embedding_v*/
learned_stopwords_v*.json

# Secrets. The pre-existing "env/" rule matches a DIRECTORY only - a real
# .env file was not covered and would have been committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
